what was the file name for the fine grained sudo escalation we created 

The file we created for fine-grained sudo escalation was:

/etc/sudoers.d/zerosix


It contains the group-based rules for ZeroSix Solutions:

%devops → full sudo (password required)

%security → limited audit commands (journalctl, less, tail, grep) with NOPASSWD

This is the recommended way — using a file in /etc/sudoers.d/ instead of editing /etc/sudoers directly.

Do you want me to show the final contents of that zerosix sudoers file again so it’s ready to drop in?
